  "worked_solution": "Since the curve $r(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ are both parametrized by arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(s)=\\frac{1}{\u03ba(s)}=\\frac{1}{\u2016{T}^{\u2032}(s)\u2016}\n$$\n\nWe differentiate $T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and calculate its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{\u2032}(s) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061s)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\u27e8-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061s,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061s,\\,-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061s\u27e9 \\\\ \u2016{T}^{\u2032}(s)\u2016 & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{(-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061s)}^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061s)}^{2}+{(-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061s)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{cos}^{2}\u2061s+{cos}^{2}\u2061s+2{sin}^{2}\u2061s} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2{cos}^{2}\u2061s+2{sin}^{2}\u2061s} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2({cos}^{2}\u2061s+{sin}^{2}\u2061s)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of curvature is\n\n$$\nR(s)=\\frac{1}{\u2016{T}^{\u2032}(s)\u2016}=\\frac{1}{1}=1.\n$$",
